// @vibex/wasm_wat_encoder — WAT text → core-wasm binary compiler; the
// single-fn `compile` surface (ADR-0070 Phase 3, #897). Pure
// `String -> Bytes`; no opaque/transparent type surface of its own.
//
// `version` was `export let version = "0.0.1"` directly in the old
// index.vibe facade — a real importable binding, not just contract
// metadata — preserved as an implementation-file value (wat_encoder.vibe)
// with a matching bodyless declaration here (Codex review precedent, PR
// #914). No other value aliases existed in the old facade.
//
// wat_encoder_test.vibe used to pull `compile` in via a literal-filename
// `import ./index.vibe {...}` of this package's own facade; it was
// retargeted to `import ./wat_encoder.vibe {...}` once this contract
// replaced index.vibe. The parent-dir lib/@vibex/wasm/
// {spec_control,spec_i32}_test.vibe already import this package in
// directory form (`import ./wat_encoder {...}`), which resolves to this
// contract unchanged. (No bench file in this package.)

